    "interpretation": "Read this as a software-parity result on clinical pilot data, not a quantum advantage claim. On this held-out split the quantum feature map is statistically indistinguishable from the dimension-matched LINEAR control (+0.0237 accuracy, McNemar p=0.2632) and is statistically indistinguishable from the dimension-matched NONLINEAR control (-0.0079 accuracy, McNemar p=0.7905) \u2014 which is the expected and honest outcome for 4 qubits, a shallow ansatz, and a few hundred clinical reference samples. What is demonstrated is that the hybrid path runs end-to-end and is measurable against a fair classical control, not that quantum helps."
